# near-stocks NEAR MAINNET deployment config.
#
# This is a reference template, not something any service reads directly. Copy the values you need
# into whatever actually injects env vars for your real deployment (ECS task definition / AWS
# Secrets Manager / Parameter Store) — the same way services/oracle's own buildspec.yml deploys it.
# local/common.env (gitignored) is the equivalent file for the LOCAL dev stack against NEAR
# testnet; this file is its mainnet counterpart, tracked so the real values are documented and
# reviewable, minus every secret (never committed — see the SECRETS section at the bottom).
#
# Deployed 2026-09-27: near-stocks.near, contract code deployed at mainnet block 217514100
# (tx 59Cjgj2ZFSMdB5A59q4D8MyTkBMFWv9kq9p2gCcWZYYs). Owner=treasury and guardian=sequencer are both
# NEAR implicit accounts (Nightly wallets) — see nearchain/cmd/nsmainnet/deploy.go for the exact
# account ids; not repeated here as inline comments since they're already public on-chain and in
# that file, this template just references them by role.

# ── Core NEAR identity (contractUtils.NEAR_STOCKS_MAINNET_ACCOUNT/_CHAIN_ID and
#    nearchain.USDCMainnet already default to these exact values in code — set them explicitly here
#    anyway for clarity and to survive a future code change to those defaults) ──
NEAR_NETWORK=mainnet
NEAR_RPC_URL=https://rpc.mainnet.fastnear.com
NEAR_STOCKS_ACCOUNT=near-stocks.near
NEAR_USDC_CONTRACT=17208628f84f5d6ad33f0da3bbbeb27ffcb398eac501a31bd6ad2011e36133a1
NEAR_BROKER_ID=2

# ── Roles (public account ids — safe to commit; the same accounts must exist and be funded before
#    services using them are started) ──
NEAR_TREASURY_ACCOUNT=8f4015265b9b67afca2ebbfd81c82e10b2a75e68c28916943f724b2068e30d15
NEAR_SEQUENCER_ACCOUNT=9bce340bdc623a5fca6d12ca6ab3f49a42e2a1eac97d648339dd0209bff26946

# ── Withdraw guard (api-server) — same default as testnet unless you want a different real-money
#    cap; this bounds the size of a single hot-wallet-signed treasury withdrawal ──
NEAR_WITHDRAW_MAX_USDC=1000

# ── Indexer (services/indexer-server) — start at the contract's own deploy block so it doesn't
#    walk all of mainnet history looking for near-stocks.near events that can't exist before this.
#    NEARDATA_URL can be left unset: sink.go already defaults to https://mainnet.neardata.xyz
#    whenever NEAR_NETWORK != "testnet". Get a NEARDATA_API_KEY before real traffic — the free tier
#    rate-limited (429s) even under testnet's much lighter load (see pre-mainnet-contract-review).
NEAR_INDEXER_START_BLOCK=217514100
# NEARDATA_API_KEY=

# ── Oracle (api-server, engine, liquidation, amm, cron-server all read this) — point at a real,
#    reachable production oracle. services/oracle (vendored from 100exhange-oracle) is confirmed
#    working for TSLA/NVDA/AAPL/GOOGL; if you're running it via this repo's own ./backend.sh
#    locally that's http://localhost:8097, but a real deployment needs this served from somewhere
#    every other service can actually reach (not localhost) — see the ORACLE_SERVER_URL discussion
#    in the mainnet deployment conversation for the two real options (existing standalone oracle's
#    AWS deployment, or adding services/oracle to this repo's own CI/CD).
ORACLE_SERVER_URL=

# ── SPY only (nearchain/cmd/nsmainnet list-stocks) — Ondo's SPYon/USD Chainlink feed on Ethereum
#    mainnet. Get the exact proxy address from https://data.chain.link (docs.chain.link and
#    data.chain.link both blocked automated lookup when this was written — do not guess this).
SPY_CHAINLINK_FEED=
# ETH_RPC_URL=https://ethereum-rpc.publicnode.com   # free public RPC; only needed for SPY pricing

# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECRETS — NEVER put real values here or in any tracked file. Listed so it's clear what exists.
# ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# NEAR_SEQUENCER_KMS_KEY_ID   Recommended for real mainnet (nearchain/kms.go already supports AWS
#                             KMS signing) — the sequencer signs every batch submission continuously,
#                             so it's the highest-exposure key in the system.
# NEAR_SEQUENCER_PRIVATE_KEY  The plaintext fallback ("ed25519:...", explicitly documented in
#                             nearchain/kms.go as "testnet and local only") — only used if
#                             NEAR_SEQUENCER_KMS_KEY_ID isn't set. Source: your own secrets manager,
#                             or local/near-credentials/mainnet/9bce...6946.json's private_key field
#                             for local testing only.
# NEAR_TREASURY_PRIVATE_KEY   Only needed if api-server signs treasury actions directly (optional —
#                             withdrawals can run without it, see nearFunding.service.go). Source:
#                             local/near-credentials/mainnet/8f40...0d15.json's private_key field.
